# Code owners — GitHub auto-requests these reviewers on matching PRs.
#
# Per-zone ownership. Everything is @qiuethan for now; as people are hired,
# add them to the relevant line. Owners are space-separated, and you must keep
# the existing owner if they are to stay one:
#
#     /services/team-tracking/ @qiuethan @somebody
#
# NOTE: last matching pattern wins and is NOT cumulative — for a given file
# only the last line it matches applies, so writing `/services/llm/ @somebody`
# on its own silently REMOVES @qiuethan as owner of that zone rather than
# adding to it. There is no error when this happens; you just stop being asked
# to review.
#
# Requesting is not gating: `require_code_owner_reviews` is off on staging, so
# GitHub asks the owner for a review but any approval satisfies the branch
# protection. Code owners are not requested on draft PRs, and an owner without
# write access to the repo is silently ignored — codeowners-valid.yml fails the
# build on that second case.
#
# "Zone" is the repo's word for these buckets; docs/CODE-OWNERSHIP.md defines
# them. Older comments say "area" for the same thing.
#
# See issue #34 (Code Reviewer Assigner + Discord webhook).

# Fallback: anything not covered by a zone below. This is what owns the `root`
# zone — the top-level files (README.md, AGENTS.md, Makefile, pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, the dotfiles). `root` cannot have a line of its own: it is not a
# directory.
* @qiuethan

# Catch-alls for workspace members that have no zone of their own yet — the
# `services/other` and `packages/other` zones.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, and it is the OPPOSITE of pr-zone-check.yml. CODEOWNERS is
# last-match-wins, so these two lines must sit ABOVE the specific ones below:
# a file in services/llm/ matches both, and the later, more specific line is
# the one that applies. Move them below and they would swallow every service.
#
# Without these, an unregistered service resolved to the `*` fallback instead
# of anyone who knows it. check-labels.mjs enforces both their presence and
# their position.
/services/                       @qiuethan
/packages/                       @qiuethan

# Zones — keep in sync with zone_for() in .github/workflows/pr-zone-check.yml.
/discord-bot/                    @qiuethan
/packages/auth/                  @qiuethan
/services/connectors/            @qiuethan
/services/documentation-system/  @qiuethan
/services/gateway/               @qiuethan
/services/llm/                   @qiuethan
/services/meeting/               @qiuethan
/services/team-tracking/         @qiuethan
/services/verification/          @qiuethan
/docs/                           @qiuethan
/scripts/                        @qiuethan
